+
+### Dashboard credential publication (Task14 repair, 2026-10-27)
+
+Dashboard and gateway coordinate through the same `tenants.conf.lock` first-byte advisory lock
+(Windows msvcrt / POSIX flock). The shared configuration directory must support this coordination
+file. Startup readers wait for publication to finish; live authentication uses a nonblocking lock.
+A `tenants.conf.pending` marker means a transaction
+or reconciliation has not been confirmed: gateway startup refuses the file instead of accepting
+possibly orphaned credentials. Dashboard startup or a subsequent successful mutation reconciles
+from committed SQLite state. A process crash releases the OS lock; the pending marker remains
+until reconciliation. This is a publication/compensation protocol, not a cross-filesystem database
+transaction or an assurance about power-loss durability.
+
+Parser errors for both environment and file mappings never include the original credential.
+Unchanged legacy credentials continue to work, including an omitted/null cube defaulting to user.
+File-backed credentials reload automatically before each authenticated request. Changes to
+MEMOS_TENANTS environment variables still require a process restart.
+
+### Automatic credential reload
+
+The verifier checks the file identity, size, nanosecond modification/change times and pending
+marker on every authentication request. An unchanged publication is not reparsed. Changes are
+read under the shared publication lock and swapped as a complete in-memory snapshot; disk work
+runs off the async event loop. No watcher process, management endpoint or new dependency is needed.
+
+- Dashboard key creation works on the next request after its successful publication; revocation
+  rejects subsequent requests, including requests made by already-connected MCP clients.
+- A rename does not change the credential publication or interrupt its authorization.
+- A missing, unreadable, malformed, conflicting or pending file temporarily disables file-backed
+  credentials instead of retaining potentially revoked keys. Environment-backed identities remain
+  available. A later confirmed publication automatically recovers without a restart.
+- An empty file stays authenticated: it does not silently turn off authentication. Environment
+  identities are independent; removing a duplicate file entry does not revoke its environment copy.
+- Requests already authorized may finish; reload does not cancel their side effects. Unchanged
+  public health/landing endpoints do not trigger a reload and reflect the latest auth snapshot.
+- Deploying this code requires one initial gateway restart. Afterwards dashboard key publication
+  needs no gateway restart. All workers detect the shared file independently on their next request.
+
+Regression: `python -m pytest test_gateway_live_reload.py test_gateway_tenants_file.py
+test_gateway_contract.py test_gateway_tools.py -q` (from this directory).
